the fork fold (plan step 1: "a handler that can end early becomes one action per path; other branches become
conditional effects"; reader.py chose one action per path instead):
method: the kept actions of one label that end the same way are grouped: the same path end and the same
continuation (the events the path leaves: unit, wait point, Esc or not), counted with and without the same lists of
locals (without, the args: write differs and becomes a conditional effect). Paths whose fact preconditions overlap
differ only in non-fact tests (replay checks) and cannot become conditions on facts, so each group is split greedily
into sub-groups of pairwise disjoint paths. A sub-group becomes one action: a key with one set on every path stays a
precondition; on keys that differ the union stays a precondition (left out when it is the whole domain) and each
path's own sets become the condition of its effects; an effect every path has stays unconditional when the paths
cover the union, else it is conditional too. rel.count_ops on the result (task.write_sas's rules, PRODUCT_LIMIT 64).
Two versions. Strict: only paths that end in a yield are folded. A yield names its site (the wait points of the next
events), so these are paths that meet again; this is step 1's rule. Every end: also paths that end the handler (end,
stopped, chained, room, parked) with the same end kind. The record keeps the end's kind, not its site, so this joins
an early return with the last one, which step 1 keeps apart.
