== 4. what else multiplies the count by 2 or more ==
method: per kept action, the product of its precondition sets of more than one value (after cutting them to the
domain and leaving out a set that holds for every value) and the product of its guessed values (task._expand's
rules; an action past PRODUCT_LIMIT 64 counted once for guesses). "Operators gone if that set were one" is
operators x (1 - 1/size), summed over the actions with that set. Full recounts with rel.count_ops.
  per-path forks: 71,324 actions from 8,984 labels (x7.9). The fold above takes them to 19,039 (every end) or
    27,308 (strict).
  guessed values: x4.09 on top of the precondition sets (144,904 variants become 592,866 before variants with no
    effect are dropped; 583,602 counted). Almost all of it is the dialog verb slots that local:220 writes as
    guesses (VerbOps on a slot the reader cannot work out). Operators gone if that guess were one operator:
    verb:127 224,505; verb:126 146,790; verb:128 146,790; verb:120 115,722; verb:121 114,588; verb:122 113,076;
    verb:125 52,050; verb:124 51,042; verb:123 50,382; var:52 12,085; var:53 11,920; every other key under 400.
    With every guess through pick variables (task.py's PRODUCT_LIMIT 1): 142,913 operators (73 pick, 32 pick
    variables), 1,638,560 effects. PRODUCT_LIMIT 8: 193,691 operators.
  precondition sets of more than one value: x2.03 (144,904 variants from 71,324 actions). var:53, the input state
    (VAR_USERPUT > 0 is {1, 2, above}): x3 on 29,952 actions, 67,407 operators gone if it were one. cutscene depth
    ({1..5}): x5 on 2,699 actions, 35,300. No other key. Cutting each set to the values reachable from the start
    changes nothing (232,209 operators either way on the usable actions).
  lists of locals per wait point (args:): events x5.1 (255,302 operators; 50,316 if each point kept its largest list
    only); Esc x6.7 (226,618; 33,947).
  "~frozen" sentence and walk variants: exactly x2 on sentences and walks (50,556 operators).
  under x2: sentences on inventory objects (4,384 of 28,060), two-object sentences (7,596 of 28,060), dialog line
    variants per VAR_VERB_SCRIPT value and room (273 actions).
How they stack in local:220: one Esc input (a wait point and a list of locals) forks into up to 320 paths on the
dialog's facts, and each path carries 2 to the power of its guessed verb slots in operators.

